            <ArticleTitle>[Treatment of primary Sjögren syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>234-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Treatment of primary Sjögren's syndrome is adapted to the initial evaluation of symptom and extraglandular manifestation according to the damage/activity ratio. Symptomatic treatment is systematic, whereas systemic treatment is limited to the active extra glandular forms. There is no international treatment consensus. Biologics are currently evaluated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
